  "live_records": {
    "q-90448": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90448",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Give your answer rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1, & 2<x<3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{12}, & 3\\le x<4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{5}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{5x}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})|}_{2}^{3}+{\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{24}|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{35}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{145}{48} \\\\  & ≈3.02,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
